You are a senior research-infrastructure reviewer. Review the code-framework design document acot_note/1004_code_framework.md (Chinese) for the repository in the current directory (UAV language-specified target tracking in CARLA; offline training under train/ and carla_uav_tracking/rollout/opening_*.py; closed-loop evaluation via carla_uav_tracking/rollout/{policy.py,policy_server.py,run_rollout.py,env.py,metrics.py,eval_asd.sh} and launchers runs/asd/iter/launch_wd.sh, runs/opening_dump/*.sh, runs/tah_v90/*.sh; analysis scripts carla_uav_tracking/rollout/{iter_gate,opening_ds,opening_cl,arch_compare,deploy_compare,tah_need}.py).

Goal of the design: one entry point per stage (data/prep/train/eval/analyze) so that different methods/arms differ only by configuration, eliminating configuration inconsistencies; versioned protocol; provenance; compatibility checks (FOV, tick interval, feature extractor); GT-channel fencing; seed registry; results keyed by (experiment, arm, seed); strangler migration with parity tests.

Please verify the document AGAINST THE ACTUAL CODE (read the files; cite file:line):
1. Completeness of the §5 mapping: does it cover EVERY behaviour-affecting configuration channel (all policy_server.py argparse flags, run_rollout.py flags, every os.environ read in carla_uav_tracking/rollout/*.py and scene/*.py, eval_asd.sh shell knobs, JSON configs ASD_CFG/TRK_CFG/OPENING_CFG keys, hard-coded behaviour constants)? List anything missing or mis-mapped.
2. Feasibility and safety of the strangler approach (translator resolved-config -> legacy flags/env) and the parity acceptance criteria per phase; are the criteria sufficient to guarantee no silent behaviour change? CARLA is not fully deterministic.
3. GT fencing (§6): is the classification of privileged perception vs diagnostic vs logging-only channels correct and complete given the code?
4. Offline side (§8): dataset manifests, mandatory splits, content-addressed caches, compat checks (fov_deg, tick_s, feature id), legacy artefact import; does it address the known failures (70°/90° FOV mismatch, 0.2 s vs 0.6 s TAH sampling, missing split manifest, config_v5_fov90 sharing output dirs, opening ckpts under eval_out)?
5. Results/analysis (§7, §9): per-seed results, tick logs with seed, unified metrics/stats, legacy result import; any correctness traps (e.g. skipped episodes, partial files, scorer gt_idx bug, commit_k coupling)?
6. Python 3.8 constraint on the CARLA client side, docker/container constraints (no new docker networks; containers must use the existing cyh-carla-net), coordination with another concurrent session editing env.py/policy.py.
7. Over-/under-engineering, phase ordering, effort estimates, missing pieces (e.g. DAM4SAM service management, data generation spec, test-seed locking, how 1004 re-runs use the framework).

